From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ncrypt: PKCS #8 for EC keys, encrypted and imported.

NCryptExportKey(PKCS8_PRIVATEKEY) of a P-256/P-384 key gave a PrivateKeyInfo only in the clear;
under a secret (NCRYPTBUFFER_PKCS_SECRET, NCRYPTBUFFER_PKCS_ALG_OID) it was NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED.
It is now encrypted with PBES2 like an RSA key's (the encryption is shared). NCryptImportKey of a
PKCS #8 blob knew RSA only: an EC PrivateKeyInfo (id-ecPublicKey, RFC 5915 ECPrivateKey with its
public point), plain or encrypted, is imported as a BCRYPT_ECCPRIVATE_BLOB (ECDSA). .NET's
Export/ImportEncryptedPkcs8PrivateKey and ImportPkcs8PrivateKey of ECDsa keys and PFX export of
EC certificates go through these.
